From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HeavyGee <gc@lockhouse.systems>
Date: Mon, 24 Nov 2026 17:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(soup): restore three RPC handlers the tip-forward merge dropped

The compose's test gate failed with

  apiMachine.test.ts > rejects archive for Codex sessions outside workspace roots
  expected { error: 'Method not found' } to deeply equal
           { success: false, error: 'Codex session is outside workspace roots' }

"Method not found" means the RPC method is not registered. Three were missing
from cli/src/api/apiMachine.ts, along with their imports:

  ArchiveCodexSession   present in BOTH parents (old tip 45abeaa2b AND
                        origin/main) — an unambiguous merge loss, not a choice
  ForkArchivedCodex     upstream addition
  ListOpencodeSessions  upstream addition

MY OWN FAULT, recorded so the next seat does not repeat it. Resolving the
tip-forward conflict in this file, I dropped a ~50-line `registerHandler` block
after verifying that ONE symbol inside it (PrepareCursorImport) was already
registered elsewhere. The block carried three further registrations I never
checked. Verifying one symbol in a block does not license deleting the block.

AND THE FIRST RESTORE WAS STILL WRONG, which is the more useful half: I spliced
the handlers after the LAST registerHandler in the file, which sits inside
`setRPCHandlers()`. origin/main registers them in the CONSTRUCTOR. The test
constructs a client and never calls setRPCHandlers, so the handlers existed,
typechecked, and stayed unreachable — the same "Method not found" as before.
Present is not wired. Same shape as the imported-but-unrendered components and
the declared-but-uncalled producers this absorb keeps turning up.

WHY A HEAL, even though apiMachine.ts IS a conflicted file: rerere has the bad
resolution recorded and will replay it on every future compose. A heal applies
AFTER the merge, so it corrects the replayed state regardless. Fixing rerere's
cache instead would need the conflict to resurface first.

Retire when the merge stops dropping them (check the three registration counts
against origin/main before deleting).

VERIFIED: typecheck:cli exit 0; apiMachine.test.ts 33/33 passed, where the
failing case was the only failure in 6669 cli tests.
---
diff --git a/cli/src/api/apiMachine.ts b/cli/src/api/apiMachine.ts
index 0b540fa49..ef71a8f70 100644
--- a/cli/src/api/apiMachine.ts
+++ b/cli/src/api/apiMachine.ts
@@ -29,7 +29,10 @@ import {
     type MachineDirectoryEntry,
     type MachineListDirectoryResponse,
     type PathExistsResponse,
+    ListOpencodeSessionsRpcRequestSchema,
+    type ListOpencodeSessionsRpcResponse,
 } from '@hapi/protocol/apiTypes'
+import { ForkArchivedCodexRequestSchema } from '@hapi/protocol/apiTypes'
 import { RPC_METHODS } from '@hapi/protocol/rpcMethods'
 import { RUNNER_CAPABILITIES } from '@hapi/protocol'
 import type { RunnerState, Machine, MachineMetadata } from './types'
@@ -659,6 +662,59 @@ export class ApiMachineClient {
                 return prepared
             }
         )
+
+        // Restored 2026-11-24: the tip-forward merge of origin/main dropped
+        // these three registrations AND their imports. ArchiveCodexSession was
+        // in BOTH parents, so its loss is a merge defect, not a choice;
+        // ForkArchivedCodex and ListOpencodeSessions are upstream additions.
+        // They belong in the CONSTRUCTOR, where origin/main has them — my first
+        // restore put them in setRPCHandlers(), which apiMachine.test.ts never
+        // calls, so the handler existed and stayed unreachable ('Method not
+        // found'). Present is not the same as wired.
+        this.rpcHandlerManager.registerHandler<unknown, ArchiveCodexSessionRpcResponse>(
+            RPC_METHODS.ArchiveCodexSession,
+            async (params) => {
+                const parsed = ArchiveCodexSessionRpcRequestSchema.safeParse(params)
+                if (!parsed.success) return { success: false, error: 'Invalid Codex archive request' }
+                const sessionId = parsed.data.sessionId.trim()
+                return await archiveLocalCodexSession(sessionId, {
+                    canArchive: (session) => this.isLocalSessionWithinWorkspaceRoots(session)
+                })
+            }
+        )
+        this.rpcHandlerManager.registerHandler(RPC_METHODS.ForkArchivedCodex, async (raw: unknown) => {
+            const request = ForkArchivedCodexRequestSchema.parse(raw)
+            const { forkArchivedCodex } = await import('@/codex/shared/archivedFork')
+            return forkArchivedCodex(request, () => this.pathPolicy.allowsSpawn(request.directory))
+        })
+        this.rpcHandlerManager.registerHandler<unknown, ListOpencodeSessionsRpcResponse>(
+            RPC_METHODS.ListOpencodeSessions,
+            async (params) => {
+                const parsed = ListOpencodeSessionsRpcRequestSchema.safeParse(params)
+                if (!parsed.success) return { success: false, error: 'Invalid Opencode sessions request' }
+                const rawCwd = typeof parsed.data.cwd === 'string' ? parsed.data.cwd.trim() : ''
+                if (rawCwd) {
+                    const resolvedCwd = await this.pathPolicy.resolveForCheck(rawCwd)
+                    if (!this.pathPolicy.isWithinSpawnRoots(resolvedCwd)) {
+                        return { success: false, error: 'Path is outside workspace roots' }
+                    }
+                }
+                const requestedIds = parsed.data.sessionIds ? new Set(parsed.data.sessionIds) : null
+                let allSessions
+                try {
+                    allSessions = requestedIds
+                        ? await listLocalOpencodeSessionsWithMessagesByIds(requestedIds)
+                        : await listLocalOpencodeSessionSummaries()
+                } catch (error) {
+                    return { success: false, error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Failed to read local OpenCode sessions' }
+                }
+                const sessions = []
+                for (const session of allSessions) {
+                    if (await this.isLocalSessionWithinWorkspaceRoots(session)) sessions.push(session)
+                }
+                return { success: true, sessions }
+            }
+        )
     }
 
     private async isLocalSessionWithinWorkspaceRoots(session: { cwd?: string | null }): Promise<boolean> {
